ode1 as writable primary and node2/node3 as standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"PostgreSQL 16 installed on all three nodes; node1 initialized with wal_level=replica, replication role, and pg_hba entries; node2 and node3 built via pg_basebackup -R with standby.signal and primary_conninfo pointing at node1. pg_stat_replication on node1 confirms both standbys streaming with near-zero lag, and inserted rows on node1 replicate to both standbys.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2a60f35fbaa14ed1\",\"cmd-1e2e88ea47f640d3\",\"cmd-4b22733dac644af4\",\"cmd-533a378acba54ca0\",\"cmd-6915c653dee14bac\",\"cmd-9c02a2231e284985\",\"cmd-1fa2429557ec49dc\",\"cmd-eb2845971c7f4fcf\",\"cmd-06ab1365076547bb\",\"cmd-4bc7750b9f984464\",\"cmd-b6e0fe2289e14eff\"]},{\"id\":\"failover-promotion\",\"requirement\":\"When primary is lost, a standby takes over as writable primary without losing committed data\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A row was committed on node1 and confirmed replayed on node2 (matching WAL LSN) before node1 was stopped. node2 was then promoted via pg_ctl promote, confirmed pg_is_in_recovery()=f, and a new write succeeded while all prior rows (including the last pre-failover row) remained intact — a directly observed bounded transition from healthy baseline through disruption to recovered writable state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a1add77623d6451c\",\"cmd-8869a82d6b794a4d\",\"cmd-3d2f5e87467b4bba\",\"cmd-82a59774613b4322\",\"cmd-b1bad789c8254e89\"]},{\"id\":\"remaining-standby-repoint\",\"requirement\":\"Remaining standby (node3) repointed to new primary after failover\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3's primary_conninfo was updated to node2, postgresql restarted, and pg_stat_replication on node2 confirmed node3 streaming; node3 holds the post-failover row, showing consistent data under the new topology.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-796fbd1ed6234131\",\"cmd-082804476bd04315\",\"cmd-c364a508c33b40f3\"]},{\"id\":\"former-primary-rejoin\",\"requirement\":\"Recovered former primary (node1) comes back as a standby of whichever system is primary\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1's data directory was rebuilt via pg_basebackup -R from node2 (the new primary), started with pg_is_in_recovery()=t and full data including post-failover rows, and node2's pg_stat_replication shows both node1 and node3 streaming — directly demonstrating the required recovery topology change.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-070c650445e843ff\",\"cmd-254a3259c2ff42ec\",\"cmd-14a490843ec6409d\",\"cmd-eafe822fa01a479d\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node1: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4d340bf4... and healthy standby state captured; systemctl reboot acknowledged; connection loss/reset observed during reboot; post-reboot boot_id 9c54dcf4... (changed, matches fixed after-executor snapshot); postgresql active, standby recovery mode confirmed, all data rows intact, node2 shows node1 streaming again.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3819516629aa431c\",\"cmd-0353bb34eaaa4d07\",\"cmd-4634f23fdab14895\",\"cmd-1758006f6fdf4e86\",\"cmd-16b554886f7f4380\",\"cmd-d6d8cf175a694ba7\",\"cmd-8dd1450f91654130\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node3: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4d842549... captured; reboot acknowledged with connection timeout during transition; post-reboot boot_id 26c0dbdc... (changed, matches fixed snapshot); postgresql active, standby recovery confirmed, all data present, node2 shows node3 streaming again.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8fd7a9c7b3934ed5\",\"cmd-58c311fab14a433e\",\"cmd-b0b84e1118cd43ee\",\"cmd-b113a37dc82f4233\",\"cmd-88f75b7dce1c4e7d\",\"cmd-8148d71c0e484fba\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node2 (current primary): baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state as primary\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id cce73776... with node2 confirmed primary (pg_is_in_recovery=f, 4 rows); reboot acknowledged with connection timeout/reset; post-reboot boot_id abf60f22... (changed, matches fixed snapshot); postgresql resumed active as writable primary, accepted a new write, and both node1/node3 replicated it, proving full cluster recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6eae4d49d19d4586\",\"cmd-4ff5db7464674024\",\"cmd-a7ddbae97102402c\",\"cmd-a9c7284f1e04407d\",\"cmd-5e86233cedb84425\",\"cmd-eb78169cfb694bfd\",\"cmd-f34a20749a784646\",\"cmd-a103fffe443c47ef\"]}],\"confidence\":0.93,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Building the standbys via pg_basebackup required multiple retries: two attempts timed out at the 120s proxy limit (cmd-de2e6ff211174be4, cmd-c5428130046c4e56), leading to repeated cycles of killing stray pg_basebackup/sudo processes (cmd-a9c275293d3d4aec, cmd-2a187dc4c4fd4b7b) and wiping /var/lib/pgsql/data on node2/node3 several times (cmd-72f8d5159a5344bd, cmd-3f7716a714344230, cmd-ebd2809838764461, cmd-539143eebdaf4b10, cmd-8f005afc43124045, cmd-61ce269e351e4722) before a working nohup/setsid invocation succeeded. Each of these mutations targeted only the not-yet-initialized standby data directory being built for this task (a necessary prerequisite for replication) and was fully superseded by the final successful basebackup, leaving no residue or damaged state — bounded, low-risk, and self-corrected rather than retained. Minor leftover artifacts (/tmp/pginstall.log, /tmp/basebackup.log, /root/repl_pw.txt) remain on the nodes but are benign, permission-restricted, and plausibly needed for ongoing cluster administration. No failed services, no unnecessary firewall exposure beyond the required postgresql service, and package health checks are clean on all nodes post-executor.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-de2e6ff211174be4\",\"cmd-c5428130046c4e56\",\"cmd-a9c275293d3d4aec\",\"cmd-2a187dc4c4fd4b7b\",\"cmd-72f8d5159a5344bd\",\"cmd-3f7716a714344230\",\"
